kedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T15:54:25-07:00","id":1302671,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a>, please dont make 3 separate posts in a row. and I dont want to be mean, but you are kinda beating a dead horse. I'm saying this because bot only have you decided to talk about homecoming again while bringing up the same points, but you've also decided to bring in your opinion on lessons again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T17:36:46-07:00","id":1302690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302667#post1302667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don\u2019t like that teach though fear thing in reminds my of someone beating the shit out of there famloto teach them a lesson</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of basic training. And like it or not, fear and pain <i>are</i> effective teachers. Proof: The entirety of human history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":".  Typos, of course 04-04-2019, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T18:17:50-07:00","id":1302701,"title":"","content":"Teaching through shock is effective but morally troublesome.. as it is presented in the game. The fact that Beasts embrace the Lesson Philosophy and it generally results in more ethical Beasts than those that reject it? It isn't really a celebration of lessons through shock, but an effective point of how damaging Beasts can be.<br /> <br /> Not sure what this has to do with the Homecoming though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T19:08:16-07:00","id":1302714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302701#post1302701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teaching through shock is effective but morally troublesome.. as it is presented in the game. The fact that Beasts embrace the Lesson Philosophy and it generally results in more ethical Beasts than those that reject it? It isn't really a celebration of lessons through shock, but an effective point of how damaging Beasts can be.<br /> <br /> Not sure what this has to do with the Homecoming though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh Abstinence only sex Ed the Type where IF YOU HAVE SEX YOU\u2019LL GET ALL THE AIDS is rightfuly thought of as Bullshit,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T19:11:41-07:00","id":1302715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302714#post1302714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ugh Abstinence only sex Ed the Type where IF YOU HAVE SEX YOU\u2019LL GET ALL THE AIDS is rightfuly thought of as Bullshit,</div> </div> </div> </div>I...don't understand this as a response to Arms.<br /> <br /> I mean, you're not wrong, but it has <i>nothing to do</i> with what Arms said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T19:24:18-07:00","id":1302718,"title":"","content":"Yeah... me too.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xENg4mY.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T19:46:05-07:00","id":1302720,"title":"","content":"Anyways, as far as Lessons go, it comes down a simple question: Do what the fuck ever you want and fuck anyone who gets in your way, OR you can try and be constructive and use your feeding as a means to improve people's lives as much as you can, either by being the adversity that brings out the better in them or cutting the fucker's who ain't listening down.<br /> <br /> Thing of the matter is that Beasts <i>know</i> the former is fine (enough for some, not accounting for how individuals react to it), because sating your Hunger feels good and the Horror asks for nothing else but? But it's also kind of a hollow run of things, a method of gorging mindlessly until you run into the existential question of &quot;Fuck, is this <i>it</i>?&quot; It also leaves you unarmed for any argument over the subject that could be resolved with anything more than a fist through the other person's face.<br /> <br /> And what more is that Lessons become a further means exploring the self and one's relationship to the wider world, through friends, family, and enemies both mortal and supernatural, and ultimately the environment, which directly translates into further power by Feeding Hunger, Building Lair, Discovering Atavisms, Nightmares, and Kinship benefits, and more, so it basically just helping a Beast do what they were already doing by giving essential frameworks that allow them test all of these against some kind of boundary. Like art, a Beast's path of self-discovery and self-actualization is aided by some guidelines and restrictions, and the method of working through Lessons allows for the kind of contextualization that lets a Beast <i>become</i>.<br /> <br /> And it's not like it's an either/or affair. A Beast can play at it for a while and then quit. It's not like other Beasts don't get it, even if the culture supports it.<br /> <br /> Soooooo chalk me as one of those people who think the reaction against Lessons is kind of overblown, much like the reaction against Homecoming vs Devouring.(Though in that case, for me it really just comes down to them being words, and words are cheap.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-04-2019, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T00:08:57-07:00","id":1302750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302715#post1302715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...don't understand this as a response to Arms.<br /> <br /> I mean, you're not wrong, but it has <i>nothing to do</i> with what Arms said.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> disagreed with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>'s position that shock is an effective teaching method by giving sex-ed as a counterexample.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T00:43:16-07:00","id":1302752,"title":"","content":"OK... but that's a really bad counter-example because that's not shock-teaching. That's long term indoctrination of misinformation that disguises itself in standard teaching structures. Abstinence only education isn't done like a drill sergeant breaking down fresh recruits; regardless of how we stereotype it to mock its absurdity.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't work for reasons that have nothing to do with methods: Misinformation can't beat teenage hormones... it can only confuse students on how to react. A lesson that doesn't actually work doesn't demonstrate anything about teaching methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:38:26-07:00","id":1302779,"title":"","content":"Ugh I don\u2019t think Pain and fear is a Sustainable teaching method it just breaks people. And stops them from experimenting in Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:41:30-07:00","id":1302812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302779#post1302779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh I don\u2019t think Pain and fear is a Sustainable teaching method it just breaks people. And stops them from experimenting in Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's gone through that sort of teaching mechanism a few times, I'd like to provide you with some insight:<br /> <br /> It works. You wake up before the established time every morning because you know it's coming. You have a bed ready for inspection. Your heart rate goes up when the music plays because the pain and fear and confusion are coming. The fear and pain lessen with time, in part because you adapt to avoid it and in part because you grow acclimated. You see the instructor and you leap to the proper courtesy. And they lighten up. As long as you do the things you must do, they relax the punishment.<br /> <br /> It does break you down, but it also makes you rebuild yourself. A new you in a new paradigm. And you know the pain and fear isn't forever. For you it will pass in weeks or months. You may experience again briefly once in a while, but you've evolved. You can take the pain and set it aside. You can handle the fear and push it down. The training set you up to take the stress of normalcy and then some.<br /> <br /> And then it happens to someone else. Over and over again people *volunteer* to go through it. We've used it for centuries. You say it isn't sustainable, but it is. We've changed it, fine tuned how far we can push, but it's still there. Inducing stress to make trainees more resilient.<br /> <br /> Heck even on a small scale it works. My daughter is five and cut her finger on an open can once. It's been two years and she still is very careful with sharp objects now. Because the pain of the cut on her finger and the fear on seeing that rush of red?<br /> <br /> Tldr: Yeah. Pain and fear is sustainable. It's just a matter of how you apply pain, fear, and shock and the frequency of application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:10:21-07:00","id":1302853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302779#post1302779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh I don\u2019t think Pain and fear is a Sustainable teaching method it just breaks people. And stops them from experimenting in Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, regardless of whether it is or not, the original question still stands for Beasts. They <i>can </i>just eat, but a Beast basically has to be okay with eating anyone and everyone regardless of who or what they are or what they are going through and how they can or can't afford your Satiation. Because the <i>instant</i> a Beast put in any sort of logic, any sort of reason, any sort of justification to chewing on people, they've <i>created</i> a Lesson-and most of them are going to be <i>really bad ones </i>done that way. &quot;I ate you for your [Hunger] because of X&quot; <i>invariably happens</i>.<br /> <br /> Take, for instance, death to the bourgeoisie. I think you're pretty comfortable with a Beast Sating themselves on them, in which okay, but why? If you only feed on them isn't that, in itself, a message? Isn't that, in fact, a lesson you're trying to teach? Death to the Bourgeoisie, for whatever reason you deem that correct? At a minimum, because people need to understand <i>you'll do what you want to these people, fuck off</i>?<br /> <br /> And I'm not even saying that's wrong, as specific examples go, but it is also what it is-a biased feeding that is a Beast using what they were going to do anyway to send a message to everyone else. And that's if you're lucky and manage to keep yourself only eating the bourgeoisie. Eat a member of the proletariot while sending that message, and you got some 'splaining to do, Lucy. And, if you don't have plans for meals, the likelihood of you eating someone you don't want to increases, and the more you've got to ask yourself what you're doing and why.<br /> <br /> Lessons help to keep your Hunger tamed to your will. It helps to keep you on schedule and having regularly planned meals. It acknowledges that <i>feeding</i> is <i>already</i> an <i>act of messaging</i> and that what you say <i>will eventually come back around to you</i>. Feeding changes the world, and that includes changing yourself, as you discovered when you ascended by Devouring yourself. If you want to own your Legend, own your Life, own your <i>Myth</i>, You Have To Control What The Story Is. That's what Beast is about, and Lessons are just a tool in the box that further facilitates that.<br /> <br /> Besides, there are positives. A lot of people have thoughts about Power, Hoard, Prey, Punishment, Ruin, Secrets, Transgressions that keep them from being better people, and it is possible to be gentle <i>enough</i> with a well taught feeding that the things they think they want are getting in the way of what they need, that the way they think is getting in the way they could <i>be</i>. A Beast with an eye on these things could do a lot to make a whole host of better people. If you don't believe me, consider how many people have learned to be better human beings to one another <i>through</i> horror, through things like The Twilight Zone or the darker episodes of Mushi-shi, xxxHolic and the like.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, while it can be about the ones feasted upon (And I do hope that there are always Beasts characters who attempt the art of compassionate guidance through feeding), really it comes back to the Beast owning themselves, rather than letting anyone or anything dictate who they are and what they mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:15:15-07:00","id":1302857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302812#post1302812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who's gone through that sort of teaching mechanism a few times, I'd like to provide you with some insight:<br /> <br /> It works. You wake up before the established time every morning because you know it's coming. You have a bed ready for inspection. Your heart rate goes up when the music plays because the pain and fear and confusion are coming. The fear and pain lessen with time, in part because you adapt to avoid it and in part because you grow acclimated. You see the instructor and you leap to the proper courtesy. And they lighten up. As long as you do the things you must do, they relax the punishment.<br /> <br /> It does break you down, but it also makes you rebuild yourself. A new you in a new paradigm. And you know the pain and fear isn't forever. For you it will pass in weeks or months. You may experience again briefly once in a while, but you've evolved. You can take the pain and set it aside. You can handle the fear and push it down. The training set you up to take the stress of normalcy and then some.<br /> <br /> And then it happens to someone else. Over and over again people *volunteer* to go through it. We've used it for centuries. You say it isn't sustainable, but it is. We've changed it, fine tuned how far we can push, but it's still there. Inducing stress to make trainees more resilient.<br /> <br /> Heck even on a small scale it works. My daughter is five and cut her finger on an open can once. It's been two years and she still is very careful with sharp objects now. Because the pain of the cut on her finger and the fear on seeing that rush of red?<br /> <br /> Tldr: Yeah. Pain and fear is sustainable. It's just a matter of how you apply pain, fear, and shock and the frequency of application.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, Ares. I didn't have time to formulate a more detailed explanation earlier, but you nailed it ad did so far more eloquently than i probably would have. Also, long time no talk to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 04-05-2019, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:19:20-07:00","id":1302873,"title":"","content":"To add a bit to Arc's post, something that probably doesn't get enough highlighting in the books, but something my experience has seen a few times:<br /> <br /> The Lesson isn't always for the Beast's direct victim. One of the more interesting ways I've seen a balance struck between Lessons and more vicious in feeding Beasts, is who they're trying to help. It's one thing to be a Beast that feeds viciously on horrible people and assuages themselves that it's OK because of who their victims were. It's another to go beyond that and use the death of an abuser to insert yourself into your victims' victims lives and help them come out stronger. It's not fantastic, it's manipulative and creepy, but it's at least trying to pull a net good out of it.<br /> <br /> While not a new take or anything, consider how much better a place like Gotham would be if Bruce Wayne put more of his resources into fighting poverty, homelessness, and food insecurity, than into punching criminals as Batman. Not that he needs to stop being Batman and getting his emotional need for revenge out on whatever criminals need punching tonight, but actually put his vast resources to fighting crime instead of fighting criminals.<br /> <br /> It feels like a place that's narratively ripe for Beasts to find compromise even if their normal feeding strategies aren't great for more compassionate lessons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:49:43-07:00","id":1302886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302873#post1302873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add a bit to Arc's post, something that probably doesn't get enough highlighting in the books, but something my experience has seen a few times:<br /> <br /> The Lesson isn't always for the Beast's direct victim. One of the more interesting ways I've seen a balance struck between Lessons and more vicious in feeding Beasts, is who they're trying to help. It's one thing to be a Beast that feeds viciously on horrible people and assuages themselves that it's OK because of who their victims were. It's another to go beyond that and use the death of an abuser to insert yourself into your victims' victims lives and help them come out stronger. It's not fantastic, it's manipulative and creepy, but it's at least trying to pull a net good out of it.<br /> <br /> While not a new take or anything, consider how much better a place like Gotham would be if Bruce Wayne put more of his resources into fighting poverty, homelessness, and food insecurity, than into punching criminals as Batman. Not that he needs to stop being Batman and getting his emotional need for revenge out on whatever criminals need punching tonight, but actually put his vast resources to fighting crime instead of fighting criminals.<br /> <br /> It feels like a place that's narratively ripe for Beasts to find compromise even if their normal feeding strategies aren't great for more compassionate lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.<br /> <br /> The nutshell here is that You Know Who You Are, <i>What</i> You Are, now the big question is how are you going to apply yourself, and to what end. As a broad concept, Beast isn't about actualization so much as transcendence, in the practical, Maslow's Hierarchy of Needs sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:52:11-07:00","id":1302887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302873#post1302873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not a new take or anything, consider how much better a place like Gotham would be if Bruce Wayne put more of his resources into fighting poverty, homelessness, and food insecurity, than into punching criminals as Batman. Not that he needs to stop being Batman and getting his emotional need for revenge out on whatever criminals need punching tonight, but actually put his vast resources to fighting crime instead of fighting criminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one comes up a fair bit in relation to Batman, and honestly it depends on which take on Batman you mean - some takes certainly <i>do</i> try to put the Wayne resources towards helping others as well as going out there to fight criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T12:39:56-07:00","id":1302902,"title":"","content":"I know, it's a comic book example, and thus prone to variations based on authors, and so on.<br /> <br /> But archetype Batman lives in archetype Gotham, which is a city plagued by crime because it's a city that is consistently portrayed as having a non-functional social safety net to justify the city being that bad. Archetype Batman has super expensive equipment that is only possible because Bruce Wayne is just that rich.<br /> <br /> Comics don't care too much about reality, they don't have to, they're fun regardless. But Batman's annual budget is so big that Bruce Wayne could literally afford to pay the whole budget of most US cities with it. I don't mean be a philanthropist. I mean he could pay every city worker's salary, cover all the annual expenses, etc. He has to be that insanely rich. Fixing Gotham's social safety net is something he isn't doing. He has far, far too much power to 'try' and fail unless he's not really trying.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:43:15-07:00","id":1302917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302873#post1302873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add a bit to Arc's post, something that probably doesn't get enough highlighting in the books, but something my experience has seen a few times:<br /> <br /> The Lesson isn't always for the Beast's direct victim. One of the more interesting ways I've seen a balance struck between Lessons and more vicious in feeding Beasts, is who they're trying to help. It's one thing to be a Beast that feeds viciously on horrible people and assuages themselves that it's OK because of who their victims were. It's another to go beyond that and use the death of an abuser to insert yourself into your victims' victims lives and help them come out stronger. It's not fantastic, it's manipulative and creepy, but it's at least trying to pull a net good out of it.<br /> <br /> <b>While not a new take or anything, consider how much better a place like Gotham would be if Bruce Wayne put more of his resources into fighting poverty, homelessness, and food insecurity, than into punching criminals as Batman. Not that he needs to stop being Batman and getting his emotional need for revenge out on whatever criminals need punching tonight, but actually put his vast resources to fighting crime instead of fighting criminals.</b><br /> <br /> It feels like a place that's narratively ripe for Beasts to find compromise even if their normal feeding strategies aren't great for more compassionate lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out that Bruce Wayne did in fact try this, and it failed spectacularly because ...well...people are assholes, especially in Gotham. He even got embarassed pretty badly for making the same mistake as his philanthropist parents and thinking he'd somehow do better.<br /> <br /> Edit: OH! The lesson <i>Bruce</i> learned was: Some problems need to be solved with violence and fear. Not a bad lesson to learn, and not untrue in many cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 04-05-2019, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:54:06-07:00","id":1302920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302917#post1302917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should point out that Bruce Wayne did in fact try this, and it failed spectacularly because ...well...people are assholes, especially in Gotham. He even got embarassed pretty badly for making the same mistake as his philanthropist parents and thinking he'd somehow do better.<br /> <br /> Edit: OH! The lesson <i>Bruce</i> learned was: Some problems need to be solved with violence and fear. Not a bad lesson to learn, and not untrue in many cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how Arkham is a revolving door?<br /> <br /> It might be less of one if, after some of the initial work as Batman, Bruce stopped emphasing the Dark Knight and putting more into the infrastructure of Gotham, including investments into better practices and security for Arkham. Instead, he buys a new Batmobile.<br /> <br /> Bruce is kind of bad at planning, and &quot;because assholes&quot; isn't really a good answer to <i>his</i> failures to do even the most minor of actions to handle things.<br /> <br /> Archetypal Batman isn't interested in building a better Gotham, he's interested in punishing criminals, and because of that, nothing ever actually happens for the state of Gotham. Assholes can be dealt with, particularly with THAT ABSURD of a budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:02:55-07:00","id":1302921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302920#post1302920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how Arkham is a revolving door?<br /> <br /> It might be less of one if, after some of the initial work as Batman, Bruce stopped emphasing the Dark Knight and putting more into the infrastructure of Gotham, including investments into better practices and security for Arkham. Instead, he buys a new Batmobile.<br /> <br /> Bruce is kind of bad at planning, and &quot;because assholes&quot; isn't really a good answer to <i>his</i> failures to do even the most minor of actions to handle things.<br /> <br /> Archetypal Batman isn't interested in building a better Gotham, he's interested in punishing criminals, and because of that, nothing ever actually happens for the state of Gotham. Assholes can be dealt with, particularly with THAT ABSURD of a budget.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, i'd actually like to see a story arc where the necessary measures to make Arkham well and truly inescapable were enacted. I imagine it'd take some pretty draconian measures, some real heavy-duty guards and superhuman mental health experts. And probably a lot of human and civil rights violations - not that Bruce has any problem with either of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:17:13-07:00","id":1302925,"title":"","content":"well its sorta a good good story for a eshmaki with hunger for punishment. a beast who takes care of the problem in the short term to satiate his hunger, but never will stop the problem in the long term because it would make his job a lot harder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:25:58-07:00","id":1302927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302921#post1302921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You know, i'd actually like to see a story arc where the necessary measures to make Arkham well and truly inescapable were enacted. I imagine it'd take some pretty draconian measures, some real heavy-duty guards and superhuman mental health experts. And probably a lot of human and civil rights violations - not that Bruce has any problem with either of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, yeah. Long before Batman basically did irreversible damage? Not as much.<br /> <br /> This is the point. Batman played Batman way longer than he should have. Batman <i>always</i> plays Batman more than he should. Batman <i>doesn't appreciate the power </i>Bruce Wayne has to <i>stop crime in Gotham</i>, not until it's too late. Batman was great at creating windows for Bruce Wayne to do some real good, but he'd rather be a god damned bat punishing criminals than building a better Gotham and actually playing against the fundamental problems. Batman would be more successful if both of his sides actually played more at being a crime lord, honestly.<br /> <br /> Which is all to say that Batman is a quintessential Hero-a short-sighted ego-driven dumbass with too many weapons and more interest in punching a motherfucker than actually building a place where people aren't so god damned mother-fuckery.<br /> <br /> (I don't like Batman, can you tell.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:34:16-07:00","id":1302930,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t like the the whole teaching Though fear thing It shows that it was a late addition. I loved the Homecoming and not have society except anything at all of me.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s called the DEVOURING and involves A monster eating your soul! For GodMachines\u2019s Sake,<br /> <br /> I know souls aren\u2019t your personality in COfD but still it takes what\u2019s supposed to by A private Awakening to your true self.<br /> <br /> And takes it from a Creepy person Noticing you from the dreamscape Stalking you and indoctrinated you to a Terrorist cult,all Beasts are terrorists now,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 04-05-2019, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:38:44-07:00","id":1302932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302930#post1302930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t like the the whole teaching Though fear thing It shows that it was a late addition. I loved the Homecoming and not have society except anything at all of me</div> </div> </div> </div>Soooooooooo don't use Lessons, use Homecoming.<br /> <br /> Easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:41:15-07:00","id":1302933,"title":"","content":"Yeah but it still Hurts me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:47:20-07:00","id":1302934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302933#post1302933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but it still Hurts me</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's on you. At some point, the way to stop things from hurting is to let go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T15:11:50-07:00","id":1302938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302934#post1302934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's on you. At some point, the way to stop things from hurting is to let go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen. Like the song says: Let it go, let it go. You'll feel better when you do, and probably find a new approach you like as much or more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1301237#post1301237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But how long do you hold on to the past and continue letting it define you and your perspective before it becomes incredibly harmful?<br /> -Me</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:55:06-07:00","id":1302958,"title":"","content":"On the whole Batman thing:<br /> <br /> I'm generally amused at how easily Batman can either be a great inspiration for an Eshmaki or Ugallu Nemesis... or a particularly experienced Hero. Though there's a lot that depends on which version of the character we're talking about.<br /> <br /> Though I admit the Nemesis side of thing would be more compelling if they'd stop resetting the rogue gallery (not that DC would) so that the ones that have retired from crime on some level (Penguin spent time as a mostly legit business owner and information broker, Bane gave up on crime after he came to grips with his feelings about the Bat, a good number of them have moved more towards anti-heroes than villains). The idea that Batman's utterly relentless campaign to foil criminals through violence works by making the relatively sane ones just stop after they realize they can't out-obsess Batman is interesting regarding the idea of lessons. The fact that the comic industry is so dominated by &quot;return to the status quo&quot; thinking that they constantly undo that only makes Bruce look that much more the guy getting his rocks off beating up criminals and not caring about helping his city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302930#post1302930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t like the the whole teaching Though fear thing It shows that it was a late addition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's OK not to like stuff. It's not mandatory. As in literally it isn't mandatory in-game. Beasts that don't try to do it don't have any magical force come down and smite them; only the logical consequences of whatever they do instead.<br /> <br /> And it shows it was a late addition because we saw it being added. If you never say the drafts before lessons came in, especially with Beast's development issues, I doubt you would actually notice it as opposed to just blame it on the disjointedness that came from the poor finalization of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I loved the Homecoming and not have society except anything at all of me. </div> </div> </div>OK, but you've ignored some big issues with your statements about it.<br /> <br /> And Beasts still had societies in the Homecoming era drafts. They just made less sense because there wasn't a clear in-universe path towards how they came together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s called the DEVOURING and involves A monster eating your soul! </div> </div> </div>The Homecoming metaphysically was the same thing: a monster Soul ate your human soul, and turned you into a combined entity. Homecoming sounds nicer (even though it makes no sense to the process described), but it doesn't change what happens during the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but still it takes what\u2019s supposed to by A private Awakening to your true self. </div> </div> </div>The Devouring is still a private act in the end. Other Beasts can facilitate (like having a therapist identify your diagnosis), but can't force it to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And takes it from a Creepy person Noticing you from the dreamscape Stalking you and indoctrinated you to a Terrorist cult,all Beasts are terrorists now, </div> </div> </div>This is a gross misrepresentation of things. You can like Homecoming better just because you do. You don't need to manufacture stuff to justify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:53:22-07:00","id":1302975,"title":"","content":"Why where the lessons bullshit added,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T18:01:47-07:00","id":1302976,"title":"","content":"because used to, the game had really nothing to add to feeding. it was literally just &quot;you feed and heroes want to kill you for it&quot;. lessons brought context to it because of complaints of pointless feeding (and before you bring up vampire, vampire has a lot of things with feeding such as territories to make it have nuance). yup, lessons were partially brought in due to complaints","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T18:46:28-07:00","id":1302979,"title":"","content":"In Beast terms I have always seen Batman as Ugallu Nemesis, though now that you mention it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Eshmaki would make a good fit as well, while Joker would be a Namtaru Ravager. Batman would be a Beast less interested in lessons and more about feeding his hunger while Joker is determined to teach the Bat a lesson about ruin.<br /> <br /> But as always YMMV.<br /> <br /> About the actual topic personally I preferred Homecoming both as a term and as the default way for Beasts to become what they are but I\u2019m largely over it by now especially with the PG closing the gap further. I still prefer the term though. Similarly I feel the lessons are a bit redundant especially as a larger social thing amongst the begotten but again the matter is kinda small and easy to handle case by case at each table. I also preferred Soul to Horror as a term but again it\u2019s no big deal. These are merely preferences and ones that have no real impact on the actual mechanics of the game and thus can be easily handled at each table or even for each individual Beast. One might see the Horror as just that while other feels, and sees, it as his/her Soul, for one the moment of becoming a Beast felt like being devoured and changed by a monster while to another it felt like a Homecoming. One tries to teach lessons while feeding another feeds with abandon while the third couldn\u2019t care less about lessons but feeds on those s/he feels are deserving of it because of a personal code and tries to keep a low profile to avoid heroes.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m just rambling but it is way too late and I should have been sleeping hours ago so there is that.<br /> <br /> Enjoy Beast as the excellent game it is and try not to fret over the minor differences at each table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T19:04:00-07:00","id":1302982,"title":"","content":"Well, this thread has improved my view on lessons a lot. Still not gonna frequently use em, but use of nightmares as deterrents might be more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:43:06-07:00","id":1303398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302982#post1302982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this thread has improved my view on lessons a lot. Still not gonna frequently use em, but use of nightmares as deterrents might be more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good way to handle it, in my experience. Most every Beast i've played mainly did...well, things relevant to their personal goals. Lessons only came into play when 'teachable moments' presented themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:56:15-07:00","id":1303405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302958#post1302958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you never say the drafts before lessons came in, especially with Beast's development issues, I doubt you would actually notice it as opposed to just blame it on the disjointedness that came from the poor finalization of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite funny. I only read the final version. I vaguely knew something had been added, but I really wouldn't have guessed at Lessons, they seem pretty integral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T14:51:51-07:00","id":1303410,"title":"","content":"Here it is <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOGZvcHh3V19rSms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7F...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T08:55:31-07:00","id":1303537,"title":"","content":"Lessons tend to be pretty integral to my beasts personally, and I honestly glossed over the devouring and how it went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T11:04:01-07:00","id":1303567,"title":"","content":"So since it hasn't been addressed, I wanna take some of my time to answer a question here, being why Lessons were added in.<br /> <br /> The answer to that is actually kind of really easy, because it's the same reason Mages became occult detectives and Sin-Eaters became social justice necromancers (for the win)-because while it's nice to assume otherwise, most players kind of suck at self-motivation, which is a key element of good character design.<br /> <br /> Mage is probably the better poster child of the issue than Geist, since Geist at least had the &quot;What was your life missing before and how are you going to fix that now&quot; going on, plus the question of what, at least, was your attitude towards the dead-but both were games that gave you a lot of power and a recontextualization for your life, but nowhere to neccesarily go. Sure, they pointed at things-Mage was all about chasing after the hidden symbols of power in the world and using that to grow and develop, and Geist had the above, but it wasn't....explicit text in the original versions, that left a lot of people with characters with really cool powers and nothing to do but enact their own will.<br /> <br /> Now for any sufficiently self-motivated player, creating a similar character is not hard, but RPG convention actually still leans heavily on the idea that a player character is an unmoored reactor to the hooks provided by the game master. Even after all the time that White Wolf has spent honing an audience on that subject, there's still a lot of people who just don't come up with a personal ambition. So these games (and others aside) honed down into the idea of a thing to do-Mages now explicitly chase Mysteries (and in so doing, grow in magical power), and Geists have their Krewe Archetypes to direct them towards resolving issues for the dead and ultimately challenging the Underworld. By making the <i>action</i> more of a point, these games got their points across stronger and gave an answer for players asking &quot;What are we gonna do tonight, Brain?&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast, in the middle of the Kickstarter campaign, clearly had a problem of this sort. Sure, it was clear that Beasts build their Lair and chase after their Hungers and Kinship, but a lot of people reading at the time had no fucking clue to what end. With a desperate attempt to right the ship middle of the campaign rather than pull back, the revisions that changed a lot of things also introduced Lessons as something that both united Beasts into a culture and gave them something to do-it's the same as before, ultimately, but now it has a strong contextualization, something that kind of screams &quot;Build Your Myth&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's more hit or miss than what happened in the case of Mage or Geist, but a significant part of the reader group* at least latched onto it, and it <i>does</i> bring home the idea of building yourself, because now instead of just being a collection of things to chase and elements to grab, it makes it clear that a Beast is out to make themselves a self-owned message, fuck what anyone else thinks is being said. It's controversial as hell, but it does a decent enough job at action-izing the things a Beast was doing into a more coherent direction, ie, a story you might want to tell.<br /> <br /> It's also not a bad dynamic as it goes, because as mentioned before a Beast can change their mind about what lesson they teach or if they even bother with it. All of that goes a long way in building up the conflict with nihilism that Beast has-namely, how much worth is there in rejecting it when the value of acceptance is always there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-08-2019, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T11:52:50-07:00","id":1303579,"title":"","content":"ugh do not Dungeons and dragons the most Populur RPG in the world just have Your a adventurer ..as its hook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T11:58:05-07:00","id":1303581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303579#post1303579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ugh do not Dungeons and dragons the most Populur RPG in the world just have Your a adventurer ..as its hook</div> </div> </div> </div>Please actually read the posts you're responding to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303567#post1303567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for any sufficiently self-motivated player, creating a similar character is not hard, but <b>RPG convention actually still leans heavily on the idea that a player character is an unmoored reactor to the hooks provided by the game master.</b> Even after all the time that White Wolf has spent honing an audience on that subject, there's still a lot of people who just don't come up with a personal ambition</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T12:21:21-07:00","id":1303585,"title":"","content":"^This.<br /> <br /> Building it a little bit, Dungeons and Dragons actually makes it's point pretty explicitly, to the point where trying to diverge from it tends to be where problems really start coming up-Your gameplay is explicitly aimed at finding and clearing dungeons, with loot and murder being the point.<br /> <br /> White Wolf games, particularly Chronicles, tend to ask a little more from characters than just being a murder hobo, and that goes double for Beast, considering the main story that Beast is lampooning is, shocker, Dungeons and Dragons.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, the Lair-By-Kinship was originally a very strong element for this(hell, it actually was a combination of dungeon diving and dark mystery), but Lair-By-Hunger was kind of just left flailing in the wind. Lessons, regardless of anything else, did a good job of anchoring that back into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-08-2019, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T12:22:10-07:00","id":1303586,"title":"","content":"Also, can we all just agree that trying to use DnD to argue against elements of Beast is just inherently funny? Not to say it's invalid, just funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-08-2019, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T13:03:29-07:00","id":1303593,"title":"","content":"Hahaha Okay. That kind of was a shit comparison \u2018)<br /> <br /> I mean theirs always part of the Game to Justifies why the main characters don\u2019t just Stay home and watch TV.<br /> <br /> Like most people would do Fight Horrid monsters from another World or just Stay home , eat ice-cream, and watch Netflix. Hmmm what would you chose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T16:56:40-07:00","id":1303657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1302853#post1302853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, regardless of whether it is or not, the original question still stands for Beasts. They <i>can </i>just eat, but a Beast basically has to be okay with eating anyone and everyone regardless of who or what they are or what they are going through and how they can or can't afford your Satiation. Because the <i>instant</i> a Beast put in any sort of logic, any sort of reason, any sort of justification to chewing on people, they've <i>created</i> a Lesson-and most of them are going to be <i>really bad ones </i>done that way. &quot;I ate you for your [Hunger] because of X&quot; <i>invariably happens</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this up to a point, but a Beast feeding completely at random is still arguably teaching a lesson. &quot;Sometimes bad things happen for no other reason than that you were in the wrong place at the wrong time.&quot; Humans are wired to identify patterns; you literally can't interact with them without engaging that mental reflex, short of wiping their memories. I can see the argument for trying to control what pattern they identify to the best of your ability, but it isn't the kind of structure I've found my characters needing or wanting.<br /> <br /> That said, I prefer to get involved with other splat's problems and play up the found family angle, so I can't claim Beast, by itself, in the absence of crossover, doesn't need some kind of focus. Ironically St. George is my self motivating model. If the kingdom is too peaceful just go riding off until you run into someone in trouble!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T04:43:10-07:00","id":1303752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303567#post1303567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So since it hasn't been addressed, I wanna take some of my time to answer a question here, being why Lessons were added in.<br /> <br /> The answer to that is actually kind of really easy, because it's the same reason Mages became occult detectives and Sin-Eaters became social justice necromancers (for the win)-because while it's nice to assume otherwise, most players kind of suck at self-motivation, which is a key element of good character design.<br /> <br /> Mage is probably the better poster child of the issue than Geist, since Geist at least had the &amp;quot;What was your life missing before and how are you going to fix that now&amp;quot; going on, plus the question of what, at least, was your attitude towards the dead-but both were games that gave you a lot of power and a recontextualization for your life, but nowhere to neccesarily go. Sure, they pointed at things-Mage was all about chasing after the hidden symbols of power in the world and using that to grow and develop, and Geist had the above, but it wasn't....explicit text in the original versions, that left a lot of people with characters with really cool powers and nothing to do but enact their own will.<br /> <br /> Now for any sufficiently self-motivated player, creating a similar character is not hard, but RPG convention actually still leans heavily on the idea that a player character is an unmoored reactor to the hooks provided by the game master. Even after all the time that White Wolf has spent honing an audience on that subject, there's still a lot of people who just don't come up with a personal ambition. So these games (and others aside) honed down into the idea of a thing to do-Mages now explicitly chase Mysteries (and in so doing, grow in magical power), and Geists have their Krewe Archetypes to direct them towards resolving issues for the dead and ultimately challenging the Underworld. By making the <i>action</i> more of a point, these games got their points across stronger and gave an answer for players asking &amp;quot;What are we gonna do tonight, Brain?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Beast, in the middle of the Kickstarter campaign, clearly had a problem of this sort. Sure, it was clear that Beasts build their Lair and chase after their Hungers and Kinship, but a lot of people reading at the time had no fucking clue to what end. With a desperate attempt to right the ship middle of the campaign rather than pull back, the revisions that changed a lot of things also introduced Lessons as something that both united Beasts into a culture and gave them something to do-it's the same as before, ultimately, but now it has a strong contextualization, something that kind of screams &amp;quot;Build Your Myth&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's more hit or miss than what happened in the case of Mage or Geist, but a significant part of the reader group* at least latched onto it, and it <i>does</i> bring home the idea of building yourself, because now instead of just being a collection of things to chase and elements to grab, it makes it clear that a Beast is out to make themselves a self-owned message, fuck what anyone else thinks is being said. It's controversial as hell, but it does a decent enough job at action-izing the things a Beast was doing into a more coherent direction, ie, a story you might want to tell.<br /> <br /> It's also not a bad dynamic as it goes, because as mentioned before a Beast can change their mind about what lesson they teach or if they even bother with it. All of that goes a long way in building up the conflict with nihilism that Beast has-namely, how much worth is there in rejecting it when the value of acceptance is always there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still Hate the lessons Bullshit. It\u2019s like I\u2019m helping you by Beating the shit out of you.And Emotionally Abusing you it\u2019s for your own good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T07:08:49-07:00","id":1303772,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the &quot;lessons Bullshit&quot; is quite clearly after a few threads now something that exists 100% in your own head, and has nothing to do with what's actually in the books... so it's kinda silly to keep just going on about in threads that are supposed to be about Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T07:24:09-07:00","id":1303775,"title":"","content":"gotta agree with heavy arms. Konrad you seem to just disregard whatever input people give you on lessons. that's not a good mindset to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T08:07:23-07:00","id":1303780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303593#post1303593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahaha Okay. That kind of was a shit comparison \u2018)<br /> <br /> I mean theirs always part of the Game to Justifies why the main characters don\u2019t just Stay home and watch TV.<br /> <br /> Like most people would do Fight Horrid monsters from another World or just Stay home , eat ice-cream, and watch Netflix. Hmmm what would you chose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I choose the monsters. That's why I took the job I have. I could have sat back and said &quot;you know, I think I'll be an accountant. Bankers hours, nice office, safe from bullets.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead I chose a different profession. One where I protect people, and take down criminals and terrorists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T09:49:30-07:00","id":1303793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303752#post1303752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still Hate the lessons Bullshit. It\u2019s like I\u2019m helping you by Beating the shit out of you.And Emotionally Abusing you it\u2019s for your own good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, you asked why it was added, not how you're supposed to like it. I answered the question asked.<br /> <br /> As dealing with Hate goes, a) yes, we know, b) that's your problem at this point. I can't help you like or dislike anything, I can only explain how it works or doesn't work (and in this case, while rushed, it <i>does</i> work) and why I like it or don't.<br /> <br /> And as far as that last one goes, while I think it's more functional, fun, and interesting than people go for, and that too many people get hung up on the human perspective of it vs the perspective that Beast presents (Because yes, teaching with fear is a bad thing, but you're playing a monster who made the choice of being a monster, so at some point we're past the conventional arguments), it's not something I'm wholly married to. My Ugallu Tyrant uses them ironically, my Anakim Ravager uses it to lie to herself about her motivations, my Makara Predator and Ugallu Nemeses don't bother with them at all, and my Inguma Nemeses takes it all too seriously. I like running the gamut, and exploring the various ideas about what it means to own one's self and how that relates. I personally also really take issue with the idea of ignoring the fact that people are always saying something, and therefore like to explore the impact of that fact from different angles.<br /> <br /> I can't help you with your take on it-it's not wrong, in fairness (though, again, I think you're coming at it from the wrong angle-a lot of people do).<br /> <br /> But here's the thing-like it or not, it's part of the text. It's part of the text across several books now. Hating it doesn't change the fact that it's there. People can hate it all they want, it's still in there when I open Primordial up.<br /> <br /> So at some point, hating Lessons the way you do does nothing but basically create problems for yourself, because you're holding onto something that burns for you rather than letting go, and you're insistence on the point in the community does nothing but alienate you from that community. I say this having seen someone else fall to the same sort of problem last week.<br /> <br /> You don't like Lessons, fine, I get why, and I can't fault you for it. But if this is going to be a thing, you need to take the current corrosive impulse you have to attack it and turn it into something constructive, a way to build up and improve things for yourself and other people. If you just keep attacking Lessons when nothing's going to come of it, you're just setting yourself up to get struck down.<br /> <br /> Funny how these things come around, idn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T10:26:02-07:00","id":1303799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303752#post1303752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still Hate the lessons Bullshit. It\u2019s like I\u2019m helping you by Beating the shit out of you.And Emotionally Abusing you it\u2019s for your own good.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the above is my full response, but I have a question in contrast to this:<br /> <br /> So this is a problem as opposed to &quot;I am beating the shit out of you just because&quot; and &quot;I'ma emotionally abuse you just because?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I can point out other problems here (it's a shock of fear, not a fist to the face), but just running with the metaphor, the intentions of a person don't change anything for the person getting beaten up or abused. Put that way, if <i>that's</i> your problem, then it's not Lessons you object to, it's <i>Beast</i>(and honestly, Chronicles gamelines over all, because ain't single one of these fucks free from this sort of shit).<br /> <br /> Lesson or not, a Beast is driven to satisfy their Hunger. They perform acts of predation on people. They will <i>always </i>hunt people down and cause harm to them. To use the crass metaphors, they will beat the shit out of people and emotionally abuse the hell out of them <i>all the time</i>.<br /> <br /> And that's not out of spec for Chronicles. Vampires steal your blood and emotional will, werewolves claw at your sanity and hunt down your friends, families, and co-workers, mages will manipulate you and use you for their reality shaping schemes, Prometheans will curse your lands, lash out at you and yours, and build a toxic hatred in you, changelings will drive you to emotional extremes and fuck with your subconscious, hunters will kill and harass you and your neighbors, sin-eaters will haunt your sleep, your houses, your regrets, mummies will subjugate you and punish you, demons will destroy your stability and steal your face, and yes, Beasts will scare the fucking shit out of you.<br /> <br /> Chronicles is a game about monsters. Monsters are people who hurt people. The difference between them is how much of that is your choice, why you do it, and how you handle that personally.<br /> <br /> Vampires tend to just eventually accept the fact they hurt people. Werewolves do it in the name of shaping their territory. Mages do it in the name of shaping reality. Prometheans do it in the name of becoming more human. Changelings do it in the name of building a home for themselves. Hunters do it in the name of keeping people safe. Sin-Eaters do it in the name of helping the dead. Mummies do it in the name of their Empire and their Judges. Demons do it in the name of handling a perverse god. Sometimes, any iteration of this can include helping their victims out. A lot of the times? It leaves them on the side of the road.<br /> <br /> Beasts can do it entirely for themselves, not give a single fuck about you and how you feel, and just eat you up-beat you up and scar you because they're hungry, damn it.<br /> <br /> Or Beasts can try and think of ways to at least make it useful, to make their feeding an opportunity for you to realize, to grow, to challenge, to experience, to do <i>something more with the fact that they are going to punch your face in or scare you</i> and try and turn their Hunger into something...if not good, then at least something that doesn't completely fuck over their victims.<br /> <br /> SO which is worse?<br /> <br /> <i>Just</i> being a monster? Or being a monster trying to make something good out of what they <i>will always do</i>?<br /> <br /> Because either way, <i>Beasts hurt people</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-09-2019, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T12:10:50-07:00","id":1303811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303799#post1303799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can do it entirely for themselves, not give as single fuck about you and how you feel, and just eat you up-beat you up and scar you because they're hungry, damn it.<br /> <br /> Or Beasts can try and think of ways to at least make it useful, to make their feeding an opportunity for you to realize, to grow, to challenge, to experience, to do <i>something more with the fact that they are going to punch your face in or scare you</i> and try and turn their Hunger into something...if not good, then at least something that doesn't completely fuck over their victims.<br /> <br /> SO which is worse?<br /> <br /> <i>Just</i> being a monster? Or being a monster trying to make something good out of what they <i>will always do</i>?<br /> <br /> Because either way, <i>Beasts hurt people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Lord, what can the harvest hope for, if not for the care of the reaper man?</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T16:34:24-07:00","id":1303844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303799#post1303799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the above is my full response, but I have a question in contrast to this:<br /> <br /> So this is a problem as opposed to &quot;I am beating the shit out of you just because&quot; and &quot;I'ma emotionally abuse you just because?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I can point out other problems here (it's a shock of fear, not a fist to the face), but just running with the metaphor, the intentions of a person don't change anything for the person getting beaten up or abused. Put that way, if <i>that's</i> your problem, then it's not Lessons you object to, it's <i>Beast</i>(and honestly, Chronicles gamelines over all, because ain't single one of these fucks free from this sort of shit).<br /> <br /> Lesson or not, a Beast is driven to satisfy their Hunger. They perform acts of predation on people. They will <i>always </i>hunt people down and cause harm to them. To use the crass metaphors, they will beat the shit out of people and emotionally abuse the hell out of them <i>all the time</i>.<br /> <br /> And that's not out of spec for Chronicles. Vampires steal your blood and emotional will, werewolves claw at your sanity and hunt down your friends, families, and co-workers, mages will manipulate you and use you for their reality shaping schemes, Prometheans will curse your lands, lash out at you and yours, and build a toxic hatred in you, changelings will drive you to emotional extremes and fuck with your subconscious, hunters will kill and harass you and your neighbors, sin-eaters will haunt your sleep, your houses, your regrets, mummies will subjugate you and punish you, demons will destroy your stability and steal your face, and yes, Beasts will scare the fucking shit out of you.<br /> <br /> Chronicles is a game about monsters. Monsters are people who hurt people. The difference between them is how much of that is your choice, why you do it, and how you handle that personally.<br /> <br /> Vampires tend to just eventually accept the fact they hurt people. Werewolves do it in the name of shaping their territory. Mages do it in the name of shaping reality. Prometheans do it in the name of becoming more human. Changelings do it in the name of building a home for themselves. Hunters do it in the name of keeping people safe. Sin-Eaters do it in the name of helping the dead. Mummies do it in the name of their Empire and their Judges. Demons do it in the name of handling a perverse god. Sometimes, any iteration of this can include helping their victims out. A lot of the times? It leaves them on the side of the road.<br /> <br /> Beasts can do it entirely for themselves, not give a single fuck about you and how you feel, and just eat you up-beat you up and scar you because they're hungry, damn it.<br /> <br /> Or Beasts can try and think of ways to at least make it useful, to make their feeding an opportunity for you to realize, to grow, to challenge, to experience, to do <i>something more with the fact that they are going to punch your face in or scare you</i> and try and turn their Hunger into something...if not good, then at least something that doesn't completely fuck over their victims.<br /> <br /> SO which is worse?<br /> <br /> <i>Just</i> being a monster? Or being a monster trying to make something good out of what they <i>will always do</i>?<br /> <br /> Because either way, <i>Beasts hurt people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Goddamn i love reading your writing. Way to hit the nail right the fuck on the head, especially with ripping off that ingrained veil of innocence and moral high ground the other splats stand on when people compare them to Beast. It always has and always will drive me out of my mind how all the other splats get a pass for the awful shit they do just by being what they are while Beasts get crucified for being arguably <i>less</i> awful than many of them and far more in control. Thanks for this, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> as you have once again said what I and likely many others wanted to communicate far better than i ever could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T19:24:46-07:00","id":1303863,"title":"","content":"I still hate the devouring it feels wrong , do you know that in W:TO The Process of a Shadow Taking over the Psych is called Devouring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T19:43:54-07:00","id":1303866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303863#post1303863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still hate the devouring it feels wrong , do you know that in W:TO The Process of a Shadow Taking over the Psych is called Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>two different gamelines, two different worlds of darkness, and different meanings of &quot;Devouring&quot;. not be rude, but this proves nothing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:44:41-07:00","id":1303878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303863#post1303863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still hate the devouring it feels wrong , do you know that in W:TO The Process of a Shadow Taking over the Psych is called Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in Vampire the Masquerade Beast was the term given to the mindless berserk feeding frenzy kindred risked entering if their humanity got too low (though one of my freinds told me Gangrel tended to live there in his experience) while driven by hunger the Beghotten are hardly mindless and certainly have little to do with monster in one of the Kindred's head.<br /> <br /> Heck the Unchained make Soul Pacts all the time and that doesn't get any closer to claiming a person's soul then you would through normal murder. For added bonus there is a conversion guide because Demons are not Demons by default in Chronicles of Darkness. Not to mention there is a rather large amount of discussion on various threads about what the different levels of the Primordial Dream are refered to in CoD Mage, so not like terminology is an exclusive thing even in the same setting let alone Like Primordial Newcomer says, its not a good argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:55:32-07:00","id":1303880,"title":"","content":"I would like to add further that, as nalak42 said, Demons make SOUL PACTS. demons will take advantage of you being in a horrible state of life, making you sign a deal that will take away your very existence. Yet this is not &quot;morally black&quot; like beast scaring people to feed like they need to. In fact, soul pacts seem to be treated as morally superior to what beasts do DESPITE being an optional choice to make","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T21:50:42-07:00","id":1303889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303880#post1303880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to add further that, as nalak42 said, Demons make SOUL PACTS. demons will take advantage of you being in a horrible state of life, making you sign a deal that will take away your very existence. Yet this is not &quot;morally black&quot; like beast scaring people to feed like they need to. In fact, soul pacts seem to be treated as morally superior to what beasts do DESPITE being an optional choice to make</div> </div> </div> </div>In DtD Soul Pacts result in the utter destruction - not simply death - of the human signee. I am not sure that any other splat goes so far in damaging their mortal victims. Demons are not and never were human and do not (for the most part) aspire to be human, AFAIK. I find the game to be different in an interesting way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T00:22:18-07:00","id":1303896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1302370-why-i-really-miss-the-homecoming?p=1303863#post1303863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still hate the devouring it feels wrong , do you know that in W:TO The Process of a Shadow Taking over the Psych is called Devouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, much like before, I can neither help you like or dislike a thing, nor can I particularly help with how your brain plays word association. For me, the word Devouring covers everything from self-ascendance to that thing I keep saying I'm going to do to my roommate's Havanese mop-dog. As others have pointed out, words get used a lot of different ways. As always, about all I can do is explain why it works and why I like it.<br /> <br /> On why it works...being blunt, it's just more in tone for Beast than Homecoming. I mean, I get it, I know why a lot of people liked the power in the word, but in a game of modern supernatural horror paired up with epic mythology and fantasy couched in brutal, primordial, basic imagery and language, Homecoming (and a lot of other word choices honestly in the first draft) stick out like a sore thumb. It kept the piece from feeling cohesive, whole-which is already a problem considering how very piece meal Beast was in tone, language, attitude, etc. It's like if Star Trek always referred to their phasers as &quot;shooter things&quot;, or if a Changeling suddenly cast a Quantum Computation. Hell, referencing Demon actually puts a point there, because a lot of the initial backlash to that game <i>did </i>revolve around the fact that people couldn't reconcile their concepts of religious/mystical demons with the quantum clockwork language used to define their heavens and hells (how those concepts actually always worked better than was argued against is a subject for another day). In terms of keeping the game together and getting it to tell and feel like the story it was going to try and tell, something else <i>had</i> to come in. Problem is that there's not a lot of mythic-but-grounded-in-our-common-parlance that conveys what all that was happening when a Beast transcends their old mortality. Ah, but the literal act of change, the final threshold that one crosses-that has it's own power.<br /> <br /> I need to blur the lines here, because where my feelings on Lessons are divorced from their functionality, the reasons why I like Devouring over Homecoming are also very in line with why <i>that word</i> was what won the day.<br /> <br /> First off, it's practical. That's what happens. You have Devoured yourself-but, no, it's more than that. You have found the larger, wholer, more complete sum of self that you are, and it has confronted everything that confined you before. You have found yourself bigger, stronger, greater, fuller than your fears, your faults, your anxieties, your isolations, and you hereby assert this power over yourself and who you were by eating it. It's one part acceptance, swallowing those limitations, coming to terms with them, allowing them to nourish your future self, and one part defiance, conquest, ascendance, by consuming your weaknesses and not being poisoned by them, to gnash them between your teeth and know they've not the power to stop you. The snake has devoured it's tail and has, in so doing, proven itself to be the god it was always meant to be. How can one not come home when one has so readily come to one's self, and left everything confining behind them?<br /> <br /> And for me, that really struck a chord. Not only is it mythic and psychological and carnal-it's really just how I think of my own growth. I didn't quite realize how much I applied teeth to past versions of myself until Beast, but I had always seen growing up into a better person as a means of consuming the person I am and was. There is always a bigger fish for Sean, and that fish is the wholer, healthier, more true &quot;I&quot;. I can always be bigger than the small thing I was, I can always swallow my fears. I can so thoroughly own myself that I can feast on myself and come out stronger and wiser for it. It's actualization and transcendence.<br /> <br /> And it won't be for everyone, but I think between the existing background tone the Beast honed in on and the way it's described, it got across the sense that the Devouring is meant to be act of realization- that for the Beast?<br /> <br /> They're okay. This is who they are. That the person who was miserable and alone and confused about what was going on with them, that person is gone, fed to the person they are now. The person who has got themselves, who knows who they are? They're standing here now, with teeth lovely and sharp, tongue wet and red, and eyes sharp and knowing. That those who Devour themselves? <i>Have got this</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's me. It's not like I don't get the appeal of homecoming, of coming to a place where you are accepted regardless, but eh, it's not as....<i>powerful</i> to me. I want to know I'm okay, I want to know that <i>I accepted me</i>, that <i>I surrendered to my whole self</i>, than stress over other people making a place for me. &quot;Which way I fly is home; myself am home,&quot; to misquote Milton.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Now with that out of the way, we're also at the point of the conversation where I need to ask some questions, because the continued angle of attack to this thread is uncomfortably reminding me other people I'd rather not think about, and so it's time we get to the point:<br /> <br /> What, exactly, did you think was going to happen with this thread? What were you hoping for, how did it look going forward from the first post forward?<br /> <br /> Because as is, we know it bothers you and hurts you, and we have offered our sympathies, our understandings, and our explanations, and you still seem to want more.<br /> <br /> Soooooo what are you looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-10-2019, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}